;; A vocabulary belongs to one project, its home (2026-11-12): every
;; vocabulary is given the project that links it (by a fixed rule when several
;; do), each of its maintainers who does not maintain that project is made a
;; maintainer there, and `vocab_maintainers` goes. Code, not SQL, so each
;; vocabulary's home is an audited operation under that project, and so the
;; table rebuild can run with foreign keys off. Refuses to run while a
;; vocabulary no project links exists (see plaid.sql.vocab-home).
{:ns plaid.sql.vocab-home
 :up-fn "up"
 :down-fn "down"
 :transaction? false}
